1. Public: Members declared as public can be accessed from anywhere outside the class.

2. Private: Members declared as private can only be accessed within the same class.

3. Protected: Members declared as protected can be accessed within the same package and subclasses of the class.

4. Default (or Package-private): Members declared without any modifier have default access level, meaning they can be accessed within the same package but not outside it.

